abstract: >-
  A prospective computational study of stationary shell backreaction in a
  declared dimensionless one-field model. The fixed-reference Euclidean
  de Sitter action supplies paired metric and scalar sources for an original
  quadratic mass interaction, and both sources are updated while solving the
  regular bulk and shell junctions. The archive records the full source
  Hessian, a bounded amplitude scan, integration refinements, an independent
  acceleration-system calculation, separate proper-time endpoint checks,
  negative controls, and a distinct sampled gravitational hierarchy screen.
  The results concern static numerical closure in the chosen finite matching
  convention. They do not establish measured parameters, a rigorous existence
  or uniqueness theorem, controlled high-coupling effective field theory,
  dynamical stability, particle production, or heating. Self-consistent
  one-loop feedback does not calculate all higher-loop effects. Separate
  AI-assisted implementations and review are internal cross-checks, not
  external peer review. Reproduction requires the inherited inputs in a full
  HDBLAST checkout. Text and data use CC BY 4.0; source code uses MIT.
